    "source_excerpt": "Venlafaxine passes into breast milk. Side effects in children who are nursing have sometimes been reported. If you suspect the baby has any symptoms (being more sleepy or irritable than usual, poor feeding, trouble with gaining weight) contact the child’s healthcare provider. If there is a concern, the child’s healthcare provider can check the amount of medication in the infant’s blood."
